      "text": "Search this site Embedded Files B ring O cean and A tmosphere T ogether (BOAT) Xuanting Hao (郝轩亭) Assistant Professor Department of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering & Scripps Institution of Oceanography University of California, San Diego, 9500 Gilman Drive, La Jolla, CA 92093 Office: EBU II 580 (MAE), Keck OAR 367 (SIO) Email: x3hao@ucsd.edu The main theme of t he BOAT group is to understand the small-scale physical processes at the atmosphere–ocean interface. With the help of modern high-performance computers, we develop physics-based and data-driven models to gain insights into the lively air–sea processes. Our studies not only focus on the fundamental scientific problems in fluid mechanics, physical oceanography, and boundary layer meteorology, but also have great implications in engineering applications including weather forecasting, renewable energy harvesting, and marine infrastructure protection . Current members: Sai Pramod Anumula , PhD (MAE) Pacharadech (Tay) Wacharanan , PhD (MAE) Ehsan Goftari , PhD (SDSU/UCSD Joint Doctoral Program, co-advisor: Hanyang Li) Alexandra Redford , PhD (SIO/AOS, co-advisor: Ying-Tsong Lin) Matthew Chen , MS (MAE) Former members: Han-Hsiang (Henry) Kuo , (PhD, U of Maryland ) Dev Banthia , (PhD, Caltech ) Akanksha Gupta, (postdoc, SIO) Xiangqian Quan Hans Chen, (PhD, MIT/WHOI) Sabah Kazi , (PhD, USC) Weiyu Dang Skye Fang Report abuse Report abuse",
