      "text": "Faculty Profiles Back to Faculty Profiles Xuanting Hao Assistant Professor, Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering Fluid motions at the atmosphere-ocean interface Hao seeks to understand the small-scale fluid motions at the atmosphere-ocean interface. He builds physics-based and data-driven models of air-sea processes, such as wind turbulence, surface gravity waves and sunlight propagation – and their interactions. Applications include weather forecasting, renewable energy harvesting and marine infrastructure protection. Capsule Bio: Before joining UC San Diego in 2022, Hao was a postdoctoral associate at the University of Minnesota. He also earned his Ph.D. at the University of Minnesota. Update your profile Email: x3hao@ucsd.edu Bring Ocean and Atmosphere Together Lab Institute Affiliations: Scripps Institution of Oceanography",
